text:
The wind that blows on my cheeks,

And touches them with gentle kisses ;

Ah ! how soft are those whispers!

I feel they caress me and make me so warm;

They’re such as I would wish to hear all day long.

We have no more time, then;

For we’ve been delayed by storm or tempest,

And you may not understand me, for I am lost to all others and myself ;

But if any one should read my verse—

If any one but God Himself—

Then let it be thou.

How to write it:

1) Write a note on the back page or slip under your cover, with title and author name, that you are taking part in this competition for which ever year level you have chosen;

2) In no more than 50 words give a brief description (summary) of each picture so all may be judged fairly.

For what I am and do,
 For all you have done for me—

 O Lord, Thou hast made Thy soul free;
 And from sinless death didst set it free:
 So now to Thee my spirit cleaves;
 To Thee is joined by love sincere!
